method.description:
Get a document at index. Returns [code]null[/code] for error results. [codeblock lang=gdscript] var yaml_text = """ # Player stats name: Hero health: 100 --- # Game settings difficulty: hard enable_tutorial: false """
var result = YAML.parse(yaml_text) if !result.has_error(): var player_data = result.get_document(0) var settings = result.get_document(1)
print("Player: %s (Health: %d)" % [player_data.name, player_data.health]) print("Difficulty: %s" % settings.difficulty) [/codeblock]

Returns all documents as an [Array]. Returns an empty [Array] for error results. [codeblock lang=gdscript] var yaml_text = """ # Player stats name: Hero health: 100 --- # Game settings difficulty: hard enable_tutorial: false """
var result = YAML.parse(yaml_text) if !result.has_error(): var documents = result.get_documents()
print("Player: %s (Health: %d)" % [documents[0].name, documents[0].health]) print("Difficulty: %s" % documents[1].difficulty) [/codeblock]

Returns the number of schema validation errors. Returns [code]0[/code] if validation passed or if no validation was performed.
This is a convenience method equivalent to calling [code]get_validation_result().error_count()[/code].
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var result = YAML.parse_and_validate(yaml_text, schema)

if result.has_validation_errors():
    print("Found %d validation errors" % result.get_validation_error_count())

    # Display each error
    for i in result.get_validation_error_count():
        var error = result.get_validation_result().get_error(i)
        print("- %s" % error.message)
[/codeblock]

Returns the full [SchemaValidationResult] object containing detailed validation information. Returns [code]null[/code] if no validation was performed.
Use this method when you need access to the complete validation result API, including methods like [method SchemaValidationResult.get_all_error_paths], [method SchemaValidationResult.get_violated_constraints], and individual error inspection.
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var result = YAML.parse_and_validate(yaml_text, schema)

if result.has_validation_result():
    var validation = result.get_validation_result()

    if validation.is_valid():
        # Data is valid - safe to use
        var validated_data = result.get_data()
        process_config(validated_data)
    else:
        # Get detailed error information
        print("Validation failed at these paths:")
        for path in validation.get_all_error_paths():
            print("  - %s" % path)

        print("\nViolated constraints:")
        for constraint in validation.get_violated_constraints():
            print("  - %s" % constraint)

        print("\nFull report:")
        print(validation.get_summary())
[/codeblock]

Returns a formatted multi-line summary of all validation errors, or a success message if validation passed. Returns an empty string if no validation was performed.
This is a convenience method equivalent to calling [code]get_validation_result().get_summary()[/code].
[codeblock lang=gdscript]
var schema = YAML.load_schema_from_file("res://schemas/config.yaml")
var result = YAML.parse_and_validate(user_config_text, schema)

if result.has_validation_errors():
    # Display user-friendly error report
    show_error_dialog(result.get_validation_summary())
    # Example output:
    # Schema validation failed with 2 error(s):
    #   [1] At '/graphics/resolution': String "invalid" does not match pattern ^[0-9]+x[0-9]+$ (pattern)
    #   [2] At '/audio/volume': Value 1.5 exceeds maximum 1 (maximum)
else:
    var config = result.get_data()
    apply_config(config)
[/codeblock]
